Z||000000||Fiasco||04-12-2000||09:02 PM||||Has anyone heard of Girling, Inc.? My '85 2.8 4-spd still had the original clutch slave cylinder on it when I replaced it the other day. I re-used the 4" long dust boot and noticed it was stamped "GIRLING 34665110". I assume this to be the manufacturer and the part number. If we could get our hands on some of these, we could get quite a bit more life out of our slave cylinders. Or does anyone know of a rebuild kit that comes with this style boot? Those 1" long NAPA boots look pretty worthless.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiasco||04-13-2000||03:44 AM||||Anybody?<BR>Any ideas about a better dust boot?<BR>I read the old 4 page long thread about clutch cures that touched on this, but I don't think anyone really ever came up with anything.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||04-13-2000||03:09 PM||||I'm running a NAPA unit. have plastic tie wraped it to the slave body and the shaft. (they do get hot and melt to the slave but don't burn and are a pain to cut off)  Running AGIP DOT 5.1 fliud and have had no problem with it since october when i replaced the fluid from DOT 4 to the AGIP. I've had more problems with heat transfer than dirt and grime.  <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A>     short list of mods...   welcome to the forum! ||||reg||1
